			<div class="content" id="post-content-3789447">
									

<p>Both of these paragraphs contain the same sentence almost verbatim. It also seems odd that a purely mechanical device such as a spring-driven clock would be susceptible to electromagnetic interference. It also wouldn't explain why something like a diesel engine, which has no electrical components, so something else would have to explain why the fuel isn't combusting properly.</p>
<p>In this case, I'd recommend changing it to something along these lines.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Exploration of SCP-3292 has proven to be exceptionally difficult due to effects on technology. Electronics brought into SCP-3292 cease functionality immediately upon entry, prohibiting the use of drones. It is hypothesized that this is due to the electromagnetic fields present throughout SCP-3292. Currently, Foundation agents have mapped out approximately 35km² from SCP-3292-2.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Or, if you still want complex machinery to fail:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Exploration of SCP-3292 has proven to be exceptionally difficult due to effects on technology. Electronics and complex machinery brought into SCP-3292 cease functionality immediately upon entry, prohibiting the use of drones. It is hypothesized electronics fail due to the electromagnetic fields present throughout SCP-3292, though there is no current explanation for non-electrical machinery. Currently, Foundation agents have mapped out approximately 35km² from SCP-3292-2.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I hope this helps some. Beyond this, I think what you have is very interesting.</p>

